      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a decent start, but looking at the sentiment score it just pulled, it's actually quite low. The board is worried it's too clinical and doesn't actually tap into the \"emotion\" part of the appeal. \n\nCan you try a second version? Try to dial up the emotional impact so the positivity score is significantly higher, but—and I can't stress this enough—please don't let it become a melodrama or a giant exaggeration. I really don't want a \"cringe\" letter that sounds fake. Just... make it more moving so the score reflects the importance of the work.",
      "source": "evaluator"
